classification of the ring among \"Gemmae dubitandae\" (doubtful gems) whose 
authenticity and dating are debated, and focuses on how such objects’ 
archaeological properties and provenance affect their scholarly evaluation. The 
paper argues that clarifying these archaeological properties can lead to 
reevaluation of artifacts like the Ring of Nestor and examines how digital 
