- Key excerpts/summary:  
  - Lists the article as appearing in Oxford Journal of Archaeology, with DOI 
and pagination, confirming it is a substantial technical study rather than a 
short note.  
  - Abstract and summary (where visible) emphasize technical examination of the 
ring, adding evidence on manufacture, wear and tool marks intended to test 
whether it is a modern forgery or Bronze Age original.  
  - Confirms that Pini’s conclusions have been integrated into broader 
scholarship, serving as a reference point for subsequent debates about 
