[AIMessage → tool] create_analysis({'text': 'Lead framing and authenticity for 
the Ring of Nestor: The lead should define the Ring of Nestor neutrally as a 
gold signet ring in the Ashmolean Museum, associated with a reported Late Bronze
Age hoard said to come from a tomb near Thisbe in Boeotia, while acknowledging 
that its precise archaeological context and authenticity have been questioned. 
It should summarize Evans’s early 20th‑century attribution of the ring to a Late
Minoan I or related Bronze Age context and his interpretation of the scene as 
reflecting Minoan beliefs about the afterlife, alongside later scholarship that 
classifies the object as a "Gemma dubitanda" and discusses the possibility of a 
modern creation or reworking. The wording should avoid taking a position on 
authenticity, instead presenting the debate as an ongoing scholarly issue and 
indicating that the ring’s significance lies both in its complex iconography and
in its role in discussions of Aegean forgeries and art‑market provenances.', 
'query_id': '20260628180855273375_41cd620f'})
