{"query": {"id": "20260628180511238213_f3d004ae", "handle": "q1", "text": "“Ring
of Nestor” gold ring discovery archaeological context Mycenaean Minoan", 
"importance": "core"}, "items": [{"id": "20260628180728080940_5f4f38a6", "type":
"Evidence", "text": "The bibliographic header describes the work as: \"\"The 
ring of Nestor\". A glimpse into the Minoan after-world and a sepulchral 
treasure of gold signet-rings and bead-seals from Thisbê, Boeotia\" and locates 
it in London, 1925.", "source_ids": ["20260628180725387952_5a149ac3"], 
"citations": [12]}, {"id": "20260628180728177852_0a50be19", "type": "Evidence", 
"text": "The table of contents shows Part I titled \"Sepulchral treasure of gold
signet-rings and bead-seals from Thisbê, Boeotia\" and Part II titled \"A 
glimpse into the Minoan after-world\", indicating Evans presents the ring as 
part of a funerary hoard from Thisbe in Boeotia.", "source_ids": 
["20260628180725387952_5a149ac3"], "citations": [12]}, {"id": 
"20260628180728284797_130224c0", "type": "Evidence", "text": "Keywords attached 
to the digital record include \"Nestor; Ring; Minoan culture; Thísvi; Europe; 
Greece; Thísvi\", suggesting the ring is interpreted within Minoan cultural 
horizons despite being found in central Greece.", "source_ids": 
["20260628180725387952_5a149ac3"], "citations": [12]}, {"id": 
"20260628180728401031_cd849882", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The work is 
treated as an archaeological and iconographic study: the record classifies it 
under \"archaeological literature\" and notes several plates (\"Tafel I - V\"), 
which include photographic or drawn representations of the ring and associated 
objects.", "source_ids": ["20260628180725387952_5a149ac3"], "citations": [12]}, 
{"id": "20260628180728517520_8e4e8f36", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The title 
page describes the paper as dealing with \"Gold signet rings from Thisbe and the
'Ring of Nestor'\" and references A. J. Evans's original publication \"'The Ring
of Nestor': A Glimpse into the Minoan After-World and a Sepulchral Treasure of 
Gold Signet-Rings and Bead-Seals from Thisbê, Boeotia\".", "source_ids": 
["20260628180627952652_31025e3c"], "citations": [5]}, {"id": 
"20260628180728630649_ca3f0e57", "type": "Evidence", "text": "Hudler recalls 
Evans's narrative of discovery, stating that Evans published a group of gold 
signet rings and bead seals allegedly originating from a tomb at Thisbe in 
Boeotia and singled out one elaborate gold ring as the \"Ring of Nestor\".", 
"source_ids": ["20260628180627952652_31025e3c"], "citations": [5]}, {"id": 
"20260628180728743853_55a3291a", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The article 
situates the find in central Greece: \"Thisbê, Boeotia\" is consistently used as
the provenience, and the author notes the unusual occurrence of Minoan-style 
iconography on a ring reportedly found in a Boeotian sepulchral context.", 
"source_ids": ["20260628180627952652_31025e3c"], "citations": [5]}, {"id": 
"20260628180728852340_c39ff580", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The paper 
discusses authenticity and provenance issues, pointing out that the treasure was
acquired on the art market rather than from a documented excavation, and that 
doubts have been raised in scholarship about whether the Ring of Nestor is a 
genuine Late Bronze Age artifact or a modern forgery.", "source_ids": 
["20260628180627952652_31025e3c"], "citations": [5]}, {"id": 
"20260628180728963034_908d322d", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The abstract 
states that the paper \"presents an analysis of the iconography surrounding the 
'Ring of Nestor' in the context of Aegean forgeries and authenticity debates\" 
and aims to contribute to discourse on its significance in Minoan and Mycenaean 
art.", "source_ids": ["20260628180627919021_b2e5c47b"], "citations": [4]}, 
{"id": "20260628180729068467_d43ae065", "type": "Evidence", "text": "Eliopoulos 
notes that \"Generations of scholars have debated the genuineness of both 
Nestor's and Minos' rings\", indicating the ring is part of a wider group of 
contested Aegean signet rings.", "source_ids": 
["20260628180627919021_b2e5c47b"], "citations": [4]}, {"id": 
"20260628180729178113_1074798a", "type": "Evidence", "text": "One key claim is 
that \"The connection between incurved altars and the ring's depiction supports 
its authenticity\", referring to specific iconographic elements (altars, trees, 
possibly boats) as consistent with known Minoan religious scenes.", 
"source_ids": ["20260628180627919021_b2e5c47b"], "citations": [4]}, {"id": 
"20260628180729285389_57188b44", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The paper stresses
that contradictions in prior technical analyses make close study of the imagery 
important, and that the ring's motifs have been compared with securely 
provenanced Minoan and Mycenaean artworks to argue for or against its 
authenticity.", "source_ids": ["20260628180627919021_b2e5c47b"], "citations": 
[4]}, {"id": "20260628180729390732_860b92e4", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The 
catalog lists the full title as: \"'The ring of Nestor; a glimpse into the 
Minoan after-world, and a sepulchral treasure of gold signet-rings and 
bead-seals from Thisbê, Boeotia, by Sir Arthur Evans.\"", "source_ids": 
["20260628180725501253_8fd75c2b"], "citations": [13]}, {"id": 
"20260628180729490671_221a88ab", "type": "Evidence", "text": "Subject headings 
and description associate the work with \"Nestor (Greek mythology)\" and 
\"Minoan civilization\", showing Evans linked the ring iconographically to 
Minoan religion and mythic Nestor.", "source_ids": 
["20260628180725501253_8fd75c2b"], "citations": [13]}, {"id": 
"20260628180729593740_81c46166", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The publication 
data gives \"London, 1925\" as place and year, confirming the temporal context 
of Evans's interpretation.", "source_ids": ["20260628180725501253_8fd75c2b"], 
"citations": [13]}, {"id": "20260628180729700844_9c5b29e9", "type": "Evidence", 
"text": "The catalog notes that the work includes illustrations and plates, 
implying visual documentation of the ring and related artifacts that form the 
Thisbe treasure.", "source_ids": ["20260628180725501253_8fd75c2b"], "citations":
[13]}, {"id": "20260628180729809047_9eb0cc59", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The 
snippet mentioning the ring notes: \"Like the 'Ring of Nestor', it has a 
combination of scenes (female individual on a boat, altars, sacred trees, and 
baetyls) tied to the theme of divine ...\", indicating the typical iconographic 
elements associated with the ring.", "source_ids": 
["20260628180725546200_0e5b5e1a"], "citations": [14]}, {"id": 
"20260628180729912849_ac0c1a28", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The chapter is 
explicitly about \"Fakes and Dubitanda\", suggesting that the Ring of Nestor is 
discussed as a potentially dubious artifact and that its iconography and 
provenance are assessed critically.", "source_ids": 
["20260628180725546200_0e5b5e1a"], "citations": [14]}, {"id": 
"20260628180815085873_b988a8bd", "type": "Claim", "text": "The 'Ring of Nestor' 
is an elaborate gold signet ring that Arthur Evans presented in 1925 as the 
centerpiece of a sepulchral treasure of gold signet rings and bead seals alleged
to come from a tomb at Thisbê (Thisbe) in Boeotia, central Greece.", 
"source_ids": ["20260628180627952652_31025e3c", "20260628180725387952_5a149ac3",
"20260628180725501253_8fd75c2b"], "citations": [5, 12, 13]}, {"id": 
"20260628180815402511_e4c5511a", "type": "Claim", "text": "The treasure of gold 
signet rings and bead seals that includes the 'Ring of Nestor' was acquired on 
the art market rather than through controlled archaeological excavation, so its 
reported provenance at Thisbê, Boeotia, remains unverified and has contributed 
to doubts about the ring’s authenticity as a Late Bronze Age artifact.", 
"source_ids": ["20260628180627952652_31025e3c", 
"20260628180725546200_0e5b5e1a"], "citations": [5, 14]}], "offset": 0, "limit": 
20, "total": 23, "next_offset": 20}
